  "definition": "Bipropellant propulsion stores a fuel and an oxidiser separately and meters both into a thrust chamber. The two-stream architecture permits energetic combustion and often higher specific impulse than a comparable monopropellant system, but it adds tanks, plumbing, valves and control of mixture ratio and arrival timing.[^1]",
